A||||3||DavidHenshaw||Headlamp motor wont go off||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||10-29-2000||09:40 AM||||When I turn off the headlamps they cycle down but the motor on the left side doesn't shut off. Even with the ignition key out the headlamp motor on the left side continues to turn. What gives?<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-29-2000||11:44 AM||||You have a bad switch or dirty contacts inside you motor. Might be something else inside. Tear it down snd look. On the '84 - '86 motors I believe you can remove the switching mechanism, it's located under a small cover attached with two screws on the side of the motor and gear assy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-29-2000||11:52 AM||||Turn your headlights on (so that they stay in the upright position) and then pull the fuse..put in/ take out the fuse to operate lights as a TEMPERARY FIX until you remidy the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-30-2000||07:48 AM||||I just recently had the right motor on mine start doing the same thing. If the motor actually comtinues turning and you hear a grinding sound then most likely it is the big plastic gear. Mine has a stripped spot in it. Rodney Dickman has them. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  <P>Good Luck.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
